 "culturalNotes": "Follows the mabkhara, the incense burner of Gulf homes, made by Gulf craftspeople and used to burn oud and bakhoor. It borrows the brass stud rhythm, the flared bowl proportion and the single rising smoke line, read as household hospitality and a warm farewell, with no mystical or magical framing and no picture of a specific burner."
